{"name":"Wiener Schnitzel","hex":"#ee9900","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Wiener Schnitzel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Wiener schnitzel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Wiener_Schnitzel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wiener schnitzel","blocks":[{"text":"Wiener schnitzel, sometimes spelled Wienerschnitzel, is a type of schnitzel made of a thin, breaded, pan-fried veal cutlet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Wiener-Schnitzel02.jpg/330px-Wiener-Schnitzel02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wiener_schnitzel","wikidata":"Q6497852"},{"title":"Schnitzel","blocks":[{"text":"Schnitzel is a thin slice of meat. The meat is usually thinned by pounding with a meat tenderizer. Most commonly, the meat is breaded before frying. Breaded schnitzel is popular in many countries and is made using veal, pork, chicken, mutton, beef, or turkey. Schnitzel originated as Wiener schnitzel and is very similar to other breaded meat dishes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Breitenlesau_Krug_Br%C3%A4u_Schnitzel.JPG/330px-Breitenlesau_Krug_Br%C3%A4u_Schnitzel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schnitzel","wikidata":"Q11293688"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Wiener_Schnitzel_at_Gasthaus_Joainig_%28lightened%29.jpg/500px-Wiener_Schnitzel_at_Gasthaus_Joainig_%28lightened%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Wiener_Schnitzel_at_Gasthaus_Joainig_%28lightened%29.jpg/500px-Wiener_Schnitzel_at_Gasthaus_Joainig_%28lightened%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Wiener schnitzel served at a restauran